#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494072} :activity/id #uuid "63e75d2f-a87d-5228-8980-4d6f3fc9a47a" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048554 :topic/id #uuid "a93bb5a8-5344-5f11-a0fd-45410668ecd6" :topic/math-academy-id 1984} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494023 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493943 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c75f8c9-6d90-5e2f-9fd0-6d4f8cbd173a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨2,e,2e⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+2,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493465} {:answer/id #uuid "3050b9e4-da08-5715-ad5a-8caf10a32624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨2,-e,-2e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2,\\,z-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493472} {:answer/id #uuid "472c72f7-428a-5c92-9b64-36649f199a43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨e,1,2e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2,\\,z-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493511} {:answer/id #uuid "67d37bdf-2be9-5b4b-b6fd-993f6357958d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨1,e,-2e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2,\\,z-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493545} {:answer/id #uuid "a09c4894-0619-505a-853a-743d133d9d86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨2,e,-e⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+2,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493645}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493472} :answer-field/id #uuid "49ccc9b7-9d2d-5fab-9305-0a2ddb6c4989" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a1c45efd-b454-595e-a933-aae318d15f95" :question/math-academy-id "q-102700" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-y{e}^{z}$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-y{e}^{z})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-y{e}^{z})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-y{e}^{z}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}\\text{ }i-{e}^{z}\\text{ }j-y{e}^{z}k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,2,1) & =\\frac{2}{1}\\text{ }i-{e}^{1}\\text{ }j-(2){e}^{1}k \\\\  & =2\\,i-e\\,j-2ek \\\\  & =⟨2,-e,-2e⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,2,1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨2,-e,-2e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7ecf0ade-c143-56c2-83e7-b60005d8d75d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494028}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494027 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237932 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d8438dc-a715-5c0c-aab2-6e47f02ae119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x-y+2z-10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236008} {:answer/id #uuid "85b07a3f-7374-5a9c-b7c1-947842c86d0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x+3y+z+12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236650} {:answer/id #uuid "94a5b114-54d1-55a1-b257-cc17cc5b9faf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-y+5z-12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236759} {:answer/id #uuid "b02e51c4-263c-5a4d-80f9-9315bea2d383" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+4y-3z+15=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236937} {:answer/id #uuid "c93bc415-579e-5faf-ba97-c8c120703f69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4x+4y+5z-18=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237093}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237093} :answer-field/id #uuid "86e7ba58-6e3b-5d46-8ec2-848013d679c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237620}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a47eb1cf-14ab-540e-8110-7aec36247dcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-102711" :question/problem "Consider the surface $xy{z}^{2}=6-z.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(1,1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}xy{z}^{2} & =6-z \\\\ xy{z}^{2}+z & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)=xy{z}^{2}+z$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=6.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(1,1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy{z}^{2}+z)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy{z}^{2}+z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy{z}^{2}+z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(y{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+(x{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+(2xyz+1)\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1,2) & =(1)(2)^{2}\\text{ }i+(1)(2)^{2}\\text{ }j+(2(1)(1)(2)+1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4\\,i+4j+5\\,k \\\\  & =⟨4,4,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1,2)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,4,5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-1)+4(y-1)+5(z-2) & =0 \\\\ 4x+4y+5z-18 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8542cb45-fe3e-585c-beae-8f3803d3fd88"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494028 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366815 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "193c9497-7ea6-5a1d-b9f5-a009ce93ca23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6x-y+12z-24=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366817} {:answer/id #uuid "f29eacee-8051-57cb-aee4-51b137c18ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6x-y+z+12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366818} {:answer/id #uuid "710265a2-6141-5b27-8548-bda3797d8905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x-2y-5z+11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366819} {:answer/id #uuid "d24d01c2-6eb5-5662-b203-5deae9c0dd73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6x-3y-4z+24=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366820} {:answer/id #uuid "8c31a377-21c2-5c10-92eb-4e6439b5d5dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-y-4z+13=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366821}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366817} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac4c269d-3ccc-505a-8b3b-1f9e614487fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "baefe5d5-6705-561e-af37-627a61278732" :question/math-academy-id "q-102704" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=6{x}^{2}-y+{z}^{3}$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes  through the point where $(x,y,z)=(\\frac{1}{2},3,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(\\frac{1}{2},3,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6{x}^{2}-y+{z}^{3})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(6{x}^{2}-y+{z}^{3})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(6{x}^{2}-y+{z}^{3})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =12x\\text{ }i-\\text{ }j+3{z}^{2}k \\\\ ∇\\,f(\\frac{1}{2},3,2) & =12\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{ }i-\\text{ }j+3(2)^{2}k \\\\  & =6\\,i-\\,j+12k \\\\  & =⟨6,-1,12⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(\\frac{1}{2},3,2)\\cdot ⟨x-\\frac{1}{2},\\,y-3,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨6,-1,12⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\frac{1}{2},\\,y-3,\\,z-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 6(x-\\frac{1}{2})-(y-3)+12(z-2) & =0 \\\\ 6x-y+12z-24 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "867c6d88-e80e-5619-af3d-96e820e79d18" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494027}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494051 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323850 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28cd2801-6575-503c-8973-e5d77533e487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-2y+2z-8=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321465} {:answer/id #uuid "740d2fc5-1db2-531b-9591-8ebbee71f486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-4y+z+6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322054} {:answer/id #uuid "adb3e2fe-6b96-5d2f-a240-7193b0f2a939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-y+z-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322509} {:answer/id #uuid "c2da99c8-1b83-5384-b154-4692549ce45c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+2y-2z-12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322659} {:answer/id #uuid "c69134c6-e59d-5120-8af3-0b8bb7f8b190" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-2y+2z+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322687}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186322687} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e18b7a8-1caf-5bbf-be09-d1d09a6d4c0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1c6c7087-87b2-59e1-b5dd-8db545cc6eaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-36765" :question/problem "Consider the surface ${x}^{2}=-xyz.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(4,2,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =-xyz \\\\ {x}^{2}+xyz & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+xyz$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=0.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(4,2,-2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+xyz)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+xyz)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+xyz)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(2x+yz)\\text{ }i+xz\\text{ }j+xy\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(4,2,-2) & =(2(4)+2(-2))\\text{ }i+4(-2)\\text{ }j+4(2)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4\\,i-8j+8\\,k \\\\  & =⟨4,-8,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(4,2,-2)\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y-2,\\,z+2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,-8,8⟩\\cdot ⟨x-4,\\,y-2,\\,z+2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-4)+(-8)(y-2)+8(z+2) & =0 \\\\ 4x-8y+8z+16 & =0 \\\\ x-2y+2z+4=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b8b241c5-9ed0-5065-b6d8-8a3dd561fd54" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494023}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494072 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129596 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13a034a0-40db-53e2-8743-0500f64927fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨1,1,-e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-e,\\,y-e,\\,z-1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493426} {:answer/id #uuid "4d8e49ba-c572-585b-9000-22f731c9e31c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨e,e,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493516} {:answer/id #uuid "7fd70068-b6fc-58b5-a8fd-0b6d0f6cdc1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨1,1,-e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493590} {:answer/id #uuid "a4259989-16f4-5162-93ea-522cff1adbaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨1,1,e⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493652} {:answer/id #uuid "b48376c2-fa7d-5ea7-a3f5-9c2f64a3454e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨e,e,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y+1,\\,z+e⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493683}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493516} :answer-field/id #uuid "675858d2-09f1-5094-a85f-2db7923cff6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "39528896-10e8-5126-bdec-f26e9bdcc487" :question/math-academy-id "q-36334" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=x{e}^{y}-z$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,1,e).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,1,e):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{y}-z)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{y}-z)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{e}^{y}-z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & ={e}^{y}\\text{ }i+x{e}^{y}\\text{ }j-k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1,e) & ={e}^{1}\\text{ }i+(1){e}^{1}\\text{ }j-k \\\\  & =e\\,i+e\\,j-k \\\\  & =⟨e,e,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,1,e)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨e,e,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y-1,\\,z-e⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "f7e115a4-0109-5dcd-be67-0eff6d8c34d2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494051}}] :activity/title "Tangent Planes to Level Surfaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493376}]}
